===Glyph origin===
{{Han etyl}}
{{liushu|p}}: a lump of clay either on the ground or on a potter’s wheel. See the bottom part of the original version of [[生]] and [[丰]]. Then, the lump of clay was stylized as a vertical stroke with a black dot in the middle perhaps to avoid confusion with other characters. Eventually, the black dot turned into a short horizontal stroke. Compare the top part of 土 with the ancient version of [[十]], which is a vertical stroke with a black dot in the middle.

Unrelated to the top component of [[夌]], [[走]], and [[周]]; also unrelated to the central component of [[金]] and the overall character [[圭]].

===Etymology 1===
There is no obvious cognate and etymology, unless it may be related to {{cog|aav-pro|*tiʔ}} ({{cog|mkh-mnc-pro|*tiiʔ||soil; ground consisting of earth}}, {{cog|ssm|tɛʔ||soil; earth}}). However, this would require the assumption of a shift from front vowel to Old Chinese ''*a'' ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}).

Probably related to {{och-l|社|god of soil; altar to god of soil}}.

{{rfe|zh|Compare {{cog|mkh-vie-pro|*l-taːʔ||rock}} (> {{cog|vi|đá}})?}}

